{"title": "Best Buy brings back 4K Blu-ray discs with a slowly expanding collection", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/18/best-buy-brings-back-4k-blu-ray-discs-with-a-slowly-expanding-collection/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2020/03/Best-Buy-Store-Front.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It’s been nearly three years since Best Buy decided to ditch selling physical copies of movies, stripping its inventory from both its brick-and-mortar stores and its online catalog. But with the growing rise of 4K Blu-ray collections as a vinyl-esque collector’s item, the electronics giant has slowly begun dipping its toes back into the physical media game.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/18/best-buy-brings-back-4k-blu-ray-discs-with-a-slowly-expanding-collection/#more-738444\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-18T06:25:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-18T18:46:04.290718+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
