{"title": "YouTube ‘Co-Views’ try to guess how many people are watching your TV, rolling out now", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/17/youtube-co-views-tv/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2024/01/YouTube-Logo-google-Booth-CES-2024.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Following a change in how it counts views earlier this year, YouTube is now announcing “Co-Views” as a way for the platform to try and guess how many people are watching a YouTube video on a TV, and it counts towards the video’s total view count.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/17/youtube-co-views-tv/#more-738245\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-17T12:40:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-18T18:46:04.290718+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
