{"title": "Jensen’s exit could be Google’s TPU moment", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/17/nvidias-tough-spot-is-googles-tpu-opportunity/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2023/01/nvidia-logo-1.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Good morning. Today I’m <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenet\">rewatching Tenet</a> to better picture Robert Pattinson in his <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/film/global/robert-pattinson-new-james-bond-007-1236946655/\">new role</a>, sighing over the <a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/11/the-drone-delivery-boom-could-be-a-nightmare-for-people-traumatized-by-war/\">inevitability of delivery drones triggering PTSD symptoms</a>, and laugh-cringing at <a href=\"https://tech.yahoo.com/cybersecurity/articles/decade-old-bitly-links-were-172143275.html?guccounter=1\">some of these Bit.ly link hijack stories</a> from the weekend. Plus, prayers to anyone who had to find a last-minute hotel room during last week’s flying nightmare.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Inbox</em> is the tech newsletter that goes beyond the news cycle. We cover the most important 9to5Google stories from the last couple of days along with a few highlights from around the web. We publish every Tuesday and Thursday, and if you like what you read, <a href=\"https://9to5google.beehiiv.com/subscribe\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">please subscribe</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/17/nvidias-tough-spot-is-googles-tpu-opportunity/#more-737828\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-17T03:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-18T18:46:04.290718+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "What’s new in Android’s November 2026 Google System Updates [U: Pixel virtual gamepad]", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/november-2026-google-system-updates/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2025/01/google-play-services-1.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The monthly “<a href=\"https://support.google.com/product-documentation/answer/14343500\">Google System Release Notes</a>” primarily detail what’s new in Play services, Play Store, and Play system update across Android phones/tablets, Wear OS, Google/Android TV, Auto, and PC. Some features apply to end users, while others are aimed at developers.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/16/november-2026-google-system-updates/#more-735429\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-16T15:43:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-18T18:46:04.290718+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
